		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4832&amp;p=35533#p35533"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>[Dear VK3KYY,<br><br>Can we implement the changes you mentioned on our own radios? Specifically, you mentioned "connect the Rx audio to a spare ADC pin on the CPU." Is this feasible? If it is done, what kind of flexibility would it provide in the software?<br><br>I use the APRS feature frequently. If it can decode APRS signals, I am sure many amateur radio operators, including myself, who use OPENGD77, would perform this upgrade.<br><br>TA1ECA,<br>73</div></blockquote>We do not implement anything in OpenGD77 specifically for modified radios.<br><br>We implement GPS in OpenGD77 because some radios have an option to have an official GPS in them, then some people then fit GPS's into their radio because the firmware supports GPS.<br><br>But we don't implement anything which requires modification to all radios.<br><br>You can of course modify your own radio and modify the firmware source code to support whatever extra features you want.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sat Feb 01, 2025 10:13 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
	</entry>
