		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=4832&amp;p=35508#p35508"><![CDATA[
Has anyone else been experiencing an issue with the MD-UV380, in which the radio does not keep time?  I have three of these radios, and two of the three don't keep accurate time at all.  I'll set the time properly (I also have my UTC setting and offset set correctly), and it displays correctly when I exit and go back into the time setting (so I know my changes took effect).  If I turn off the radio and turn it back on, the time is correct.  But if I turn it off for a greater amount of time (a day or so), the next time I go to use it, it's way off (by something like one day and seven hours...this varies).  It's almost like the radio stopped tracking time while it was turned off.  I'm using firmware 20250128, but this was happening on past versions as well.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=4474">N3JAS</a> — Fri Jan 31, 2025 3:39 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
